'\" t
.TH PINTSIZE 6 "2026-11-12" "pintsize 0.1.0" "Games"
.SH NAME
pintsize \- top-down miniature racing game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pintsize
.br
.B pintsize \-\-shot
.I file.bmp target
.RI [ ticks ]
.br
.B pintsize \-\-record
.I dir target skip frames step
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Pint-Size Prix
is a top-down racing game in which thumb-sized vehicles race across
everyday places: a breakfast table, a woodworking bench, a freezer drawer,
a kitchen sink, an office desk and a backyard sandbox.
It offers a tournament, head-to-head races against the computer or a second
player on the same keyboard, and a time trial.
.PP
All graphics and sound are generated by the game while it runs.
.SH CONTROLS
.TS
l l l.
	Player 1	Player 2
Steer	Left / Right	A / D
Accelerate	Up	W
Brake / reverse	Down	S
Fire (tanks)	Right Shift	Left Shift
.TE
.PP
When playing alone, either set works, and
.B X
(accelerate),
.B Z
(brake) and
.B Space
(fire) are also available.
.TP
.B Esc
Go back, or pause during a race.
.TP
.B M
Mute sound.
.TP
.B F11
Toggle fullscreen.
.SH OPTIONS
With no arguments the game opens its window.
The following options are debugging aids that render off-screen and need no
display.
.TP
.BI \-\-shot " file.bmp target " [ ticks ]
Render a single frame to
.IR file.bmp .
.I target
is
.BR menu ,
.BI race: N\fR,
.BI h2h: N
or
.BI map: N\fR,
where
.I N
is a course number from 0 to 5.
.I ticks
(default 600) is how many simulation ticks to run first.
.TP
.BI \-\-record " dir target skip frames step"
Save a sequence of frames
.IR dir /f0000.bmp ...
for building gameplay clips.
.I target
is
.BR title ,
.BR menu ,
.BI race: N
or
.BI h2h: N\fR.
The first
.I skip
ticks are not saved, then
.I frames
frames are written,
.I step
ticks apart.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/PintSize/Prix/best.dat
Best lap times from time trials.
The location follows
.BR $XDG_DATA_HOME .
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Amir Geva.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/amirgeva/pintsize
